# Book :1060: "An unknown name, duplicate assignment to one argument, missing required argument or ordering
# violation is an error."  Here: c, which names no formal of f, after a named argument -- refused where it stands, in the binding's words.
fn: f (int: a; int: b) int
    return: a - b
int: r 0
r: f(a: 8; c: 1)
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 7; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
